    "result_text": "The acceptance suite is the entire test set, and it's fully green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `customerCode` assignment on owner creation, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**Rule:** LAST3 = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`; NNNN = a global 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to one more than the current owner count, computed before the new owner is saved.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` string field on the `Owner` response schema (alongside `displayName`/`initials`), so it's generated onto `OwnerDto` and returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `customer_code` persisted column with getter/setter.\n\n3. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added the `customer_code` column so the persisted value survives to the read-back. Tests run on `hsqldb`.\n\n4. **New step `AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 Reads the built `@Val Owner` and `OwnerRepository`, computes `last3 = lastName.substring(0, min(3, len)).toUpperCase()` and `sequence = findAll().size() + 1`, and sets `String.format(\"%s-%04d\", last3, sequence)`.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 Wired the new step into the pipeline between `build` and `save` (under the same `transaction` governance), so the count is taken before the new owner is persisted.\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` maps `customerCode` automatically by name (no annotation needed).\n\n**Verification:** `Cp09Tests` passes, and the full suite is green \u2014 `Tests run: 17, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS`. The `SMI-0007` example format and the global-sequence-increments-by-one behavior are both confirmed by the test.",
